{%- comment -%}
  Casify product page: video reviews.

  A rail of 9:16 clips customers sent in, each with its own star rating, a
  short quote and the phone it was filmed on. Clips play muted while they are
  on screen and pause when they leave; each card has its own sound button and a
  "Pause clips" switch stops them all (a clip that plays by itself must always
  be stoppable). Tapping a clip opens it large, with sound, the full review,
  and a shopping panel: the buy box's own selection, price and pack, a phone
  list, and "Add to bag".

  Three homes, one markup:
    - under the product photo, inside "The Shop Counter"
      (sections/cv-product-counter.liquid, mode 'inline'): its "Video review"
      blocks, with text from its optional "Video reviews: text" block
    - as a section of its own anywhere on a product template
      (sections/cv-pdp-video-reviews.liquid): its "Video review" blocks
    - on content pages, which have no buy box
      (sections/cv-page-video-reviews.liquid, commerce false): the same row
      and player, without the shopping panel and its "Add to bag"

  Commerce goes through the buy box ([data-cv-pdp]), the same way as the colour
  carousel: picks are sent as "cvs:choose", the panel repaints from the buy
  box's "cvs:change", and "Add to bag" submits the buy box's own form, so the
  pack and any mixed cases go in exactly as from the top of the page. Model fit
  comes first: "Add to bag" asks for the phone before it adds anything, unless
  the shopper already chose one somewhere on the page (or via a ?variant= link).

  Honest by construction: every clip, name, rating and quote is typed in by the
  merchant from a real customer review. The header score is either the
  product's own review-app rating (Shopify's reviews.rating metafields) or the
  plain average of the clips shown, labelled as such. Nothing is defaulted to a
  name, a quote or "verified": a blank clip says nothing.

  With no clips nothing renders on the storefront; the theme editor shows where
  clips will go. A clip can be limited to one product, so the default template
  can carry clips for every case.

  Shop clips (the Shop Counter's "Shop clip" blocks, shop_type): clips the shop
  made itself. They share the row and the player, and say nothing a customer
  could have said: no name, no stars, no quote, no score, no "verified". A row
  of shop clips only has its own heading ("See it in hand"), a "Shown on" stub
  in place of "Filmed on", and a "Made with AI" label on every clip ticked as
  AI-made. A shop clip is matched to its product by handle, a plain text
  compare, so the default template can carry many without loading a product.

  A shop clip can also show on every product. It then names the design it
  shows under the clip, so nobody takes it for the case on the page: the row's
  heading turns to "Our cases in hand", the page's own clip (if it has one)
  comes first, and in the player a clip of another case links to that case
  ("See this case") where this page's buy panel would be.

  Behaviour and motion: assets/cv-pdp-video-reviews.js (loaded by the layout
  when this markup is on the page). Static state: assets/cv-pdp-video-reviews.css.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% doc %}
  Renders customer video reviews: the score ticket, the clip rail and the player.

  @param {object[]} blocks - Blocks to read clips from.
  @param {string} clip_type - Block type of a clip.
  @param {string} [shop_type] - Block type of a shop-made clip: shown with no name, stars, quote or score.
  @param {boolean} [reviews] - False leaves the customer clips (clip_type) out and shows shop clips only. Default true.
  @param {object} [settings] - Text settings (a section's or a block's); defaults when absent.
  @param {string} uid - Unique id used in element ids.
  @param {string} [mode] - 'inline' for the compact row under the product photo.
  @param {boolean} [commerce] - False on templates without a buy box (content pages): the player then shows only the clip and the review, no shopping panel. Default true.
  @param {string} [attrs] - Theme editor attributes for the wrapper.
  @param {object} product - The product on the page.

  @example
  {% render 'cv-video-reviews', blocks: section.blocks, clip_type: 'review', settings: section.settings, uid: section.id, product: product %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign show_commerce = true
  if commerce == false
    assign show_commerce = false
  endif

  assign show_reviews = true
  if reviews == false
    assign show_reviews = false
  endif

  comment
    First pass: which clips belong on this product, and the totals for the score.
    Only customer clips count towards the score; shop clips have no rating.
  endcomment
  assign shown = 0
  assign review_shown = 0
  assign other_shown = 0
  assign star_sum = 0
  assign verified_count = 0
  for b in blocks
    assign kind = ''
    if b.type == clip_type
      if show_reviews
        assign kind = 'review'
      endif
    elsif shop_type != blank and b.type == shop_type
      assign kind = 'shop'
    endif
    if kind == ''
      continue
    endif
    if kind == 'shop'
      if b.settings.product_handle != blank and b.settings.product_handle != product.handle
        continue
      endif
    elsif b.settings.product != blank and b.settings.product.id != product.id
      continue
    endif
    if b.settings.video == blank and b.settings.mp4_url == blank and b.settings.mp4_asset == blank and b.settings.poster == blank and b.settings.poster_asset == blank
      continue
    endif
    assign shown = shown | plus: 1
    assign last_phone = b.settings.phone
    assign last_caption = b.settings.caption
    if kind == 'shop'
      comment
        Whose clip: the product it names ("Product in the clip"), or, when it
        names none, the product it is limited to ("Only show on").
      endcomment
      assign clip_of = b.settings.design_handle | default: b.settings.product_handle
      if clip_of != product.handle
        assign other_shown = other_shown | plus: 1
      endif
    endif
    if kind == 'review'
      assign review_shown = review_shown | plus: 1
      assign star_sum = star_sum | plus: b.settings.stars
      if b.settings.verified
        assign verified_count = verified_count | plus: 1
      endif
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    A row of shop clips only: its own heading and labels, and no score.
  endcomment
  assign only_shop = false
  if shown > 0 and review_shown == 0
    assign only_shop = true
  endif

  comment
    One shop clip under the photo: the clip sits on the left with its words
    beside it, so a single card is not left alone in a row built for several.
  endcomment
  assign solo = false
  if only_shop and shown == 1 and mode == 'inline'
    assign solo = true
  endif

  assign clip_avg = 0
  if review_shown > 0
    assign clip_avg = star_sum | times: 1.0 | divided_by: review_shown | round: 1
  endif

  comment
    The product's own rating: its Judge.me reviews (verified buyers and imported; snippets/cv-jm-verified.liquid).
  endcomment
  capture jm_stats
    render 'cv-jm-verified', mode: 'stats', scope: 'product', handle: product.handle
  endcapture
  assign jm_parts = jm_stats | split: '␟'
  assign p_count = jm_parts[0] | plus: 0
  assign use_product = false
  if p_count > 0
    assign use_product = true
    assign score = jm_parts[1] | plus: 0 | times: 1.0 | divided_by: p_count | round: 1
  else
    assign score = clip_avg
  endif
  assign score_fill = score | times: 20 | at_most: 100

  comment
    Options, found the same way as the buy box and the colour carousel.
  endcomment
  assign cvar = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign model_oi = -1
  for option in product.options_with_values
    assign oname = option.name | downcase
    if oname contains 'model' or oname contains 'phone' or oname contains 'device' or oname contains 'compatib'
      assign model_oi = forloop.index0
      break
    endif
  endfor
  if model_oi == -1
    for option in product.options_with_values
      assign fv = option.values.first | downcase
      if fv contains 'iphone' or fv contains 'galaxy' or fv contains 'pixel' or fv contains 'samsung'
        assign model_oi = forloop.index0
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
  assign style_oi = -1
  for option in product.options_with_values
    if forloop.index0 != model_oi and option.values.size > 1
      assign style_oi = forloop.index0
      break
    endif
  endfor
  assign confirmed = false
  if product.selected_variant != blank or model_oi == -1
    assign confirmed = true
  endif

  comment
    Text: from the settings passed in, or the defaults when there are none
    (the main product section without a "Video reviews: text" block).
  endcomment
  assign vr = settings
  assign shop_heading = vr.shop_heading | default: 'See it in hand'
  assign design_label = vr.design_label | default: 'Design'
  assign own_label = vr.own_label | default: 'This case'
  if only_shop
    comment
      "See it in hand" is only true of the case on the page: a row that also
      shows other cases takes the wider heading.
    endcomment
    if other_shown > 0
      assign vr_heading = vr.shop_heading_all | default: 'Our cases in hand'
    else
      assign vr_heading = shop_heading
    endif
    assign vr_lede = vr.shop_lede
    assign rail_label = vr.shop_rail_label | default: 'Case clips'
    assign hint_text = vr.shop_hint | default: 'Tap a clip to see it larger'
  else
    assign vr_heading = vr.heading | default: 'Filmed by the people who bought it'
    if other_shown > 0
      assign vr_heading = vr.shop_heading_all | default: 'Our cases in hand'
    endif
    if vr == blank
      if mode == 'inline'
        assign vr_lede = ''
      else
        assign vr_lede = 'Short clips from customers with this case on their own phone. Tap one for sound and the full review.'
      endif
    else
      assign vr_lede = vr.shop_lede | default: vr.lede
    endif
    assign rail_label = vr.rail_label | default: 'Customer video reviews'
    assign hint_text = vr.hint | default: 'Tap a clip for sound and the full review'
  endif
  assign review_bought_label = vr.bought_label | default: 'Filmed on'
  assign shop_bought_label = vr.shop_bought_label | default: 'Shown on'
  assign ai_label = vr.ai_label | default: 'Made with AI'
  if shown == 1
    assign pause_label = vr.pause_label | default: 'Pause clip'
    assign play_label = vr.play_label | default: 'Play clip'
  else
    assign pause_label = vr.pause_label | default: 'Pause clips'
    assign play_label = vr.play_label | default: 'Play clips'
  endif

  assign cta = vr.cta_label | default: 'Add to bag'
  assign cta_pack = vr.cta_pack_label | default: 'Add [qty] cases'
  assign show_was = false
  if cvar.compare_at_price > cvar.price
    assign show_was = true
    assign was_off = cvar.compare_at_price | minus: cvar.price | times: 100.0 | divided_by: cvar.compare_at_price | round
  endif
-%}

{%- if shown > 0 or request.design_mode -%}
  {{ 'cv-pdp-video-reviews.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if shown > 0 -%}
  <section class="cvvr{% if mode == 'inline' %} cvvr--inline{% endif %}{% if solo %} cvvr--solo{% endif %}" id="cvvr-{{ uid }}" data-cvvr {{ attrs }}
           data-money-format="{{ shop.money_format | escape }}"
           aria-labelledby="cvvrTitle-{{ uid }}">
    <div class="cvvr__inner">
      <header class="cvvr__head">
        <div class="cvvr__titles">
          <h2 class="cvvr__title" id="cvvrTitle-{{ uid }}" data-cvvr-split>{{ vr_heading | escape }}</h2>
          {%- if vr_lede != blank -%}
            <p class="cvvr__lede">{{ vr_lede | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- comment -%} One shop clip: its caption (the shop's own line) and what it is shown on read beside the clip, in place of the stub under it. {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if solo and last_caption != blank -%}
            <p class="cvvr__lede">{{ last_caption | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if solo and last_phone != blank -%}
            {%- assign shown_parts = last_phone | split: ' · ' -%}
            <p class="cvvr__shown">
              <span class="cvvr__shown-label">{{ shop_bought_label | escape }}</span>
              {%- for part in shown_parts -%}
                <span class="cvvr__shown-value">{{ part | escape }}</span>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- comment -%} The score is the customers' own: a row of shop clips has none. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if review_shown > 0 -%}
        {%- liquid
          if use_product
            assign score_label = vr.product_score_label | default: '[count] reviews of this case' | replace: '[count]', p_count
            if review_shown == 1
              assign score_sub = '1 on video below'
            else
              assign score_sub = review_shown | append: ' on video below'
            endif
          else
            if review_shown == 1
              assign score_label = vr.clip_score_label_one | default: 'From 1 video review'
            else
              assign score_label = vr.clip_score_label | default: 'Average of [count] video reviews' | replace: '[count]', review_shown
            endif
            assign score_sub = ''
          endif
          if verified_count > 0
            if verified_count == 1
              assign verified_line = '1 verified buyer'
            else
              assign verified_line = verified_count | append: ' verified buyers'
            endif
          endif
        -%}
        <div class="cvvr__score" data-cvvr-score role="group" aria-label="{{ score }} out of 5. {{ score_label | escape }}">
          <b class="cvvr__score-num" data-cvvr-score-num="{{ score }}" aria-hidden="true">{{ score }}</b>
          <span class="cvvr__score-side" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- render 'cv-stars', fill: score_fill, class: 'cvvr__score-stars' -%}
            <span class="cvvr__score-label">{{ score_label | escape }}</span>
            {%- if score_sub != blank or verified_count > 0 -%}
              <span class="cvvr__score-sub">
                {%- if verified_count > 0 -%}
                  <span class="cvvr__tick">{%- render 'cv-icon', name: 'user-check', size: 13 -%}</span>{{ verified_line }}
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if score_sub != blank and verified_count > 0 %} · {% endif -%}
                {{- score_sub -}}
              </span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
        </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </header>

      <div class="cvvr__wrap">
        <ul class="cvvr__rail" id="cvvrRail-{{ uid }}" data-cvvr-rail aria-label="{{ rail_label | escape }}">
          {%- assign n = 0 -%}
          {%- comment -%} Two passes: the clips of the case on the page first, then the clips of other cases. {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- for pass in (1..2) -%}
          {%- for b in blocks -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign kind = ''
              if b.type == clip_type
                if show_reviews
                  assign kind = 'review'
                endif
              elsif shop_type != blank and b.type == shop_type
                assign kind = 'shop'
              endif
              if kind == ''
                continue
              endif
              if kind == 'shop'
                if b.settings.product_handle != blank and b.settings.product_handle != product.handle
                  continue
                endif
              elsif b.settings.product != blank and b.settings.product.id != product.id
                continue
              endif
              if b.settings.video == blank and b.settings.mp4_url == blank and b.settings.mp4_asset == blank and b.settings.poster == blank and b.settings.poster_asset == blank
                continue
              endif

              assign clip_own = true
              if kind == 'shop'
                assign clip_of = b.settings.design_handle | default: b.settings.product_handle
                if clip_of != product.handle
                  assign clip_own = false
                endif
              endif
              if pass == 1 and clip_own == false
                continue
              endif
              if pass == 2 and clip_own
                continue
              endif

              assign vid = b.settings.video
              assign src_sm = ''
              assign src_lg = ''
              assign clip_ar = 0
              if vid != blank
                assign clip_ar = vid.aspect_ratio | default: 0
                comment
                  Smallest MP4 at least 480 wide for the rail, largest up to
                  1080 wide for the big player.
                endcomment
                assign best_sm_w = 99999
                assign best_lg_w = 0
                assign any_src = ''
                for source in vid.sources
                  if source.format != 'mp4'
                    continue
                  endif
                  assign any_src = source.url
                  if source.width >= 480 and source.width < best_sm_w
                    assign best_sm_w = source.width
                    assign src_sm = source.url
                  endif
                  if source.width <= 1080 and source.width > best_lg_w
                    assign best_lg_w = source.width
                    assign src_lg = source.url
                  endif
                endfor
                if src_sm == blank
                  assign src_sm = src_lg | default: any_src
                endif
                if src_lg == blank
                  assign src_lg = src_sm
                endif
              elsif b.settings.mp4_url != blank
                assign src_sm = b.settings.mp4_url
                assign src_lg = b.settings.mp4_url
              elsif b.settings.mp4_asset != blank
                comment
                  A clip kept in the theme's own assets: it travels with the
                  theme, so a preview copy and the live theme each serve theirs.
                endcomment
                assign src_sm = b.settings.mp4_asset | asset_url
                assign src_lg = src_sm
              endif

              assign poster_sm = ''
              assign poster_lg = ''
              if b.settings.poster != blank
                assign poster_sm = b.settings.poster | image_url: width: 540
                assign poster_lg = b.settings.poster | image_url: width: 1080
              elsif vid != blank and vid.preview_image != blank
                assign poster_sm = vid.preview_image | image_url: width: 540
                assign poster_lg = vid.preview_image | image_url: width: 1080
              elsif b.settings.poster_asset != blank
                assign poster_sm = b.settings.poster_asset | asset_img_url: '540x'
                assign poster_lg = b.settings.poster_asset | asset_img_url: '1080x'
              endif

              assign bought = ''
              if b.settings.phone != blank
                assign bought = b.settings.phone
              endif
              if b.settings.colour != blank
                if bought != blank
                  assign bought = bought | append: ' · '
                endif
                assign bought = bought | append: b.settings.colour
              endif

              comment
                A shop clip carries nothing a customer could have said: no name,
                stars or quote. Its words are what it shows and how it was made.
              endcomment
              assign is_shop = false
              assign clip_silent = false
              assign clip_ai = false
              assign clip_design = ''
              assign clip_url = ''
              assign clip_title = ''
              assign clip_caption = ''
              if kind == 'shop'
                assign is_shop = true
                assign who = ''
                assign clip_caption = b.settings.caption
                assign clip_design = b.settings.design
                assign clip_title = clip_design | default: shop_heading
                assign clip_label = b.settings.alt | default: clip_design | default: product.title
                assign bought_label = shop_bought_label
                if clip_own == false and b.settings.design_handle != blank
                  assign clip_url = routes.root_url | append: '/products/' | append: b.settings.design_handle | replace: '//', '/'
                endif
                if b.settings.silent
                  assign clip_silent = true
                endif
                if b.settings.ai_made
                  assign clip_ai = true
                endif
              else
                assign who = b.settings.name | default: vr.anon_label | default: 'Customer'
                assign fill = b.settings.stars | times: 20
                assign clip_label = ''
                assign bought_label = review_bought_label
              endif
            -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              A clip with no cover (an MP4 link, no cover image) loads its
              metadata and shows its own first frame (#t=0.1 makes iOS paint
              it), so the card is never a blank square before it plays.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <li class="cvvr__card{% if is_shop %} cvvr__card--shop{% endif %}{% if poster_sm == blank and src_sm != blank %} cvvr__card--bare{% endif %}" data-cvvr-card="{{ n }}" style="--i: {{ n }}" {{ b.shopify_attributes }}>
              <div class="cvvr__frame">
                {%- if poster_sm != blank -%}
                  <img class="cvvr__poster" src="{{ poster_sm }}" alt="" width="540" height="960" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
                {%- else -%}
                  <span class="cvvr__poster cvvr__poster--empty" aria-hidden="true">{%- render 'cv-icon', name: 'video', size: 40 -%}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  No poster attribute on the clip: its cover is the lazy image
                  above, which loads only as the row comes near. A video poster
                  is fetched with the page however far down the row sits.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- if src_sm != blank -%}
                  <video class="cvvr__video" data-cvvr-video muted playsinline loop
                         {% if poster_sm != blank %}preload="none"{% else %}preload="metadata"{% endif %} aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">
                    <source src="{{ src_sm }}{% if poster_sm == blank %}#t=0.1{% endif %}" type="video/mp4">
                  </video>
                {%- endif -%}
                <span class="cvvr__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></span>

                {%- if is_shop -%}
                  {%- if clip_ai -%}
                    <span class="cvvr__tag">{{ ai_label | escape }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- else -%}
                  <span class="cvvr__rate" aria-hidden="true">
                    {%- render 'cv-stars', fill: fill, class: 'cvvr__card-stars' -%}
                  </span>

                  <span class="cvvr__meta" aria-hidden="true">
                    {%- if b.settings.title != blank -%}
                      <span class="cvvr__quote">{{ b.settings.title | escape }}</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                    <span class="cvvr__who">
                      <b>{{ who | escape }}</b>
                      {%- if b.settings.verified -%}
                        <span class="cvvr__verified">{%- render 'cv-icon', name: 'user-check', size: 11 -%} {{ vr.verified_label | default: 'Verified buyer' | escape }}</span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </span>
                  </span>
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- if src_sm != blank -%}
                  <span class="cvvr__bar" aria-hidden="true"><i data-cvvr-progress></i></span>
                {%- endif -%}

                <button type="button" class="cvvr__open" data-cvvr-open aria-haspopup="dialog">
                  <span class="cvvr__sr">
                    {%- if is_shop -%}
                      {%- if src_sm != blank -%}Watch the clip{%- else -%}Open the photo{%- endif -%}: {{ clip_label | escape }}
                    {%- else -%}
                      {%- if src_sm != blank -%}Watch{%- else -%}Open{%- endif %} {{ who | escape }}’s review, {{ b.settings.stars }} out of 5 stars
                      {%- if b.settings.title != blank -%}: {{ b.settings.title | escape }}{%- endif -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </span>
                  <span class="cvvr__play" aria-hidden="true">{%- render 'cv-icon', name: 'play', size: 20 -%}</span>
                </button>

                {%- if src_sm != blank and clip_silent == false -%}
                  <button type="button" class="cvvr__sound" data-cvvr-sound aria-pressed="false">
                    <span class="cvvr__sr">{% if is_shop %}Sound for this clip{% else %}Sound for {{ who | escape }}’s clip{% endif %}</span>
                    <span class="cvvr__sound-off" aria-hidden="true">{%- render 'cv-icon', name: 'sound-off', size: 16 -%}</span>
                    <span class="cvvr__sound-on" aria-hidden="true">{%- render 'cv-icon', name: 'sound-on', size: 16 -%}</span>
                  </button>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>

              {%- comment -%}
                Under a shop clip that names its design: the design, as a link to
                that case when it is not the one on the page. Otherwise the phone
                (and colour) the clip was filmed or shown on. A shop clip's
                caption, the shop's own line and never a customer's, closes the stub.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- if is_shop and clip_design != blank and solo == false -%}
                <p class="cvvr__stub">
                  <span class="cvvr__stub-label">{% if clip_own %}{{ own_label | escape }}{% else %}{{ design_label | escape }}{% endif %}</span>
                  {%- if clip_url != blank -%}
                    <a class="cvvr__stub-value cvvr__stub-link" href="{{ clip_url }}">{{ clip_design | escape }}</a>
                  {%- else -%}
                    <span class="cvvr__stub-value">{{ clip_design | escape }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  {%- if clip_caption != blank -%}
                    <span class="cvvr__stub-note">{{ clip_caption | escape }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </p>
              {%- elsif bought != blank and solo == false -%}
                <p class="cvvr__stub">
                  <span class="cvvr__stub-label">{{ bought_label | escape }}</span>
                  <span class="cvvr__stub-value">{{ bought | escape }}</span>
                  {%- if clip_caption != blank -%}
                    <span class="cvvr__stub-note">{{ clip_caption | escape }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </p>
              {%- elsif clip_caption != blank and solo == false -%}
                <p class="cvvr__stub">
                  <span class="cvvr__stub-note">{{ clip_caption | escape }}</span>
                </p>
              {%- endif -%}

              <script type="application/json" data-cvvr-review>
                {
                  "kind": {{ kind | json }},
                  "name": {{ who | json }},
                  {%- if is_shop %}
                  "stars": 0,
                  "title": {{ clip_title | json }},
                  "own": {{ clip_own | json }},
                  "url": {{ clip_url | json }},
                  "body": {{ clip_caption | json }},
                  "verified": false,
                  "date": "",
                  "label": {{ clip_label | json }},
                  "ai": {{ clip_ai | json }},
                  "silent": {{ clip_silent | json }},
                  {%- else %}
                  "stars": {{ b.settings.stars | json }},
                  "title": {{ b.settings.title | json }},
                  "body": {{ b.settings.body | json }},
                  "verified": {{ b.settings.verified | json }},
                  "date": {{ b.settings.date | json }},
                  {%- endif %}
                  "phone": {{ b.settings.phone | json }},
                  "colour": {{ b.settings.colour | json }},
                  "boughtLabel": {{ bought_label | json }},
                  "src": {{ src_lg | json }},
                  "poster": {{ poster_lg | json }},
                  "ar": {{ clip_ar | json }}
                }
              </script>
            </li>
            {%- assign n = n | plus: 1 -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="cvvr__foot">
        <p class="cvvr__hint">
          {%- if only_shop -%}
            {%- render 'cv-icon', name: 'video', size: 15 -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- render 'cv-icon', name: 'sound-on', size: 15 -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          <span>{{ hint_text | escape }}</span>
        </p>
        <div class="cvvr__controls">
          <button type="button" class="cvvr__pause" data-cvvr-pause aria-pressed="false">
            <span data-cvvr-pause-icon="pause">{%- render 'cv-icon', name: 'pause', size: 15 -%}</span>
            <span data-cvvr-pause-icon="play" hidden>{%- render 'cv-icon', name: 'play', size: 15 -%}</span>
            <span data-cvvr-pause-label>{{ pause_label | escape }}</span>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="cvvr__arrow" data-cvvr-step="-1" aria-controls="cvvrRail-{{ uid }}">
            <span class="cvvr__sr">Previous clips</span>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 5l-7 7 7 7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="cvvr__arrow" data-cvvr-step="1" aria-controls="cvvrRail-{{ uid }}">
            <span class="cvvr__sr">More clips</span>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </button>
        </div>
        {%- if vr.submit_label != blank and vr.submit_url != blank -%}
          <a class="cvvr__submit" href="{{ vr.submit_url }}">{%- render 'cv-icon', name: 'video', size: 15 -%} {{ vr.submit_label | escape }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} The big player. Filled and run by cv-pdp-video-reviews.js. {%- endcomment -%}
    <dialog class="cvvr-lb" data-cvvr-lb aria-labelledby="cvvrLbTitle-{{ uid }}">
      <div class="cvvr-lb__inner">
        <div class="cvvr-lb__stage" data-cvvr-lb-stage>
          <div class="cvvr-lb__segs" data-cvvr-segs aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="cvvr-lb__media" data-cvvr-lb-media></div>
          <div class="cvvr-lb__tools">
            <button type="button" class="cvvr-lb__tool" data-cvvr-lb-play aria-pressed="false">
              <span class="cvvr__sr" data-cvvr-lb-play-label>Pause</span>
              <span data-cvvr-lb-play-icon="pause" aria-hidden="true">{%- render 'cv-icon', name: 'pause', size: 18 -%}</span>
              <span data-cvvr-lb-play-icon="play" aria-hidden="true" hidden>{%- render 'cv-icon', name: 'play', size: 18 -%}</span>
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="cvvr-lb__tool" data-cvvr-lb-sound aria-pressed="true">
              <span class="cvvr__sr">Sound</span>
              <span class="cvvr__sound-off" aria-hidden="true">{%- render 'cv-icon', name: 'sound-off', size: 18 -%}</span>
              <span class="cvvr__sound-on" aria-hidden="true">{%- render 'cv-icon', name: 'sound-on', size: 18 -%}</span>
            </button>
          </div>
          <button type="button" class="cvvr-lb__step cvvr-lb__step--prev" data-cvvr-lb-step="-1">
            <span class="cvvr__sr">{% if only_shop %}Previous clip{% else %}Previous review{% endif %}</span>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 5l-7 7 7 7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="cvvr-lb__step cvvr-lb__step--next" data-cvvr-lb-step="1">
            <span class="cvvr__sr">{% if only_shop %}Next clip{% else %}Next review{% endif %}</span>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="cvvr-lb__panel">
          <div class="cvvr-lb__scroll" data-cvvr-lb-scroll>
            <article class="cvvr-lb__review" aria-live="polite">
              {%- comment -%} The stars, the reviewer line and the "Made with AI" label are switched per clip by the script: a shop clip has no stars and no reviewer. {%- endcomment -%}
              <p class="cvvr-lb__rate" data-cvvr-lb-rate-row>
                <span class="cvvr-lb__stars" data-cvvr-lb-stars>{%- render 'cv-stars', fill: 100 -%}</span>
                <span class="cvvr-lb__rate-text" data-cvvr-lb-rate></span>
              </p>
              <h3 class="cvvr-lb__title" id="cvvrLbTitle-{{ uid }}" data-cvvr-lb-title></h3>
              <p class="cvvr-lb__tagline" data-cvvr-lb-tag hidden><span class="cvvr__tag cvvr__tag--ink">{{ ai_label | escape }}</span></p>
              <p class="cvvr-lb__body" id="cvvrLbBody-{{ uid }}" data-cvvr-lb-body></p>
              <button type="button" class="cvvr-lb__link cvvr-lb__more" data-cvvr-more aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cvvrLbBody-{{ uid }}" hidden>{% if only_shop %}Read more{% else %}Read the whole review{% endif %}</button>
              <p class="cvvr-lb__by" data-cvvr-lb-by>
                <b data-cvvr-lb-name></b>
                <span class="cvvr__verified cvvr__verified--ink" data-cvvr-lb-verified hidden>{%- render 'cv-icon', name: 'user-check', size: 12 -%} {{ vr.verified_label | default: 'Verified buyer' | escape }}</span>
                <span class="cvvr-lb__date" data-cvvr-lb-date></span>
              </p>
              <p class="cvvr-lb__bought" data-cvvr-lb-bought hidden>
                <span data-cvvr-lb-bought-label>{{ review_bought_label | escape }}</span>
                <b data-cvvr-lb-bought-text></b>
              </p>
              {%- comment -%} Shown by the script under a shop clip of another case, where this page's buy panel would mislead. {%- endcomment -%}
              <p class="cvvr-lb__see-row" data-cvvr-lb-see-row hidden>
                <a class="cvvr-lb__bag cvvr-lb__see" data-cvvr-lb-see href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}">{{ vr.see_label | default: 'See this case' | escape }}</a>
              </p>
            </article>

            {%- if show_commerce -%}
            <div class="cvvr-lb__buy" data-cvvr-buy>
              <div class="cvvr-lb__product">
                {%- if product.featured_image -%}
                  {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 160 | image_tag: width: 64, height: 64, alt: '', loading: 'lazy', class: 'cvvr-lb__thumb' }}
                {%- endif -%}
                <span class="cvvr-lb__pname">
                  <b>{{ product.title | escape }}</b>
                  <span data-cvvr-sel>{{ cvar.title | escape }}</span>
                </span>
              </div>
              <p class="cvvr-lb__price">
                <span class="cvvr-lb__now" data-cvvr-now>{{ cvar.price | money }}</span>
                <s class="cvvr-lb__was" data-cvvr-was{% unless show_was %} hidden{% endunless %}>{% if show_was %}{{ cvar.compare_at_price | money }}{% endif %}</s>
                <span class="cvvr-lb__off" data-cvvr-off{% unless show_was %} hidden{% endunless %}>{% if show_was %}{{ was_off }}% off{% endif %}</span>
              </p>

              {%- if style_oi >= 0 -%}
                <p class="cvvr-lb__match" data-cvvr-match hidden>
                  <span data-cvvr-match-text></span>
                  <button type="button" class="cvvr-lb__link" data-cvvr-match-pick></button>
                </p>
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- if model_oi >= 0 -%}
                {%- assign model_option = product.options_with_values[model_oi] -%}
                <label class="cvvr-lb__label" for="cvvrModel-{{ uid }}">{{ vr.model_label | default: 'Your phone' | escape }}</label>
                <span class="cvvr-lb__select" data-cvvr-select-wrap>
                  <select id="cvvrModel-{{ uid }}" data-cvvr-model aria-describedby="cvvrStatus-{{ uid }}">
                    <option value=""{% unless confirmed %} selected{% endunless %}>{{ vr.model_placeholder | default: 'Select your phone model' | escape }}</option>
                    {%- for value in model_option.values -%}
                      <option value="{{ value | escape }}"{% if confirmed and cvar.options[model_oi] == value %} selected{% endif %}>{{ value | escape }}</option>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </select>
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg>
                </span>
              {%- endif -%}

              <p class="cvvr-lb__pack" data-cvvr-pack hidden>
                <span data-cvvr-pack-text></span>
                <button type="button" class="cvvr-lb__link" data-cvvr-pack-change>{{ vr.pack_change_label | default: 'Change' | escape }}</button>
              </p>
  </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>

          {%- if show_commerce -%}
          <div class="cvvr-lb__cta">
            <button type="button" class="cvvr-lb__add" data-cvvr-add>
              <span data-cvvr-add-label>{{ cta | escape }}</span>
              <span class="cvvr-lb__add-total" data-cvvr-add-total></span>
              <svg class="cvvr-lb__tick" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12.5l4.2 4.2L19 7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="cvvr-lb__bag" data-cvvr-view-bag hidden>{%- render 'cv-icon', name: 'bag', size: 16 -%} {{ vr.view_bag_label | default: 'View bag' | escape }}</button>
            <p class="cvvr-lb__status" id="cvvrStatus-{{ uid }}" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-cvvr-status></p>
          </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        <button type="button" class="cvvr-lb__close" data-cvvr-close autofocus>
          <span class="cvvr__sr">Close</span>
          {%- render 'cv-icon', name: 'close', size: 20 -%}
        </button>
      </div>
    </dialog>

    <script type="application/json" data-cvvr-data>
      {
        "styleIndex": {{ style_oi }},
        "modelIndex": {{ model_oi }},
        "confirmed": {{ confirmed }},
        "selected": {{ cvar.options | json }},
        "variants": [
          {%- for v in product.variants -%}
            {"id":{{ v.id }},"o":{{ v.options | json }},"a":{{ v.available | json }},"p":{{ v.price }},"c":{{ v.compare_at_price | default: 0 }},"t":{{ v.title | json }}{% if v.featured_image %},"img":{{ v.featured_image | image_url: width: 160 | json }}{% endif %}}{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
          {%- endfor -%}
        ],
        "t": {
          "add": {{ cta | json }},
          "addPack": {{ cta_pack | json }},
          "adding": "Adding…",
          "added": "In your bag",
          "soldOut": "Sold out",
          "unavailable": "Choose another phone",
          "pickModel": {{ vr.pick_model_text | default: 'Pick your phone model first, so the case fits.' | json }},
          "failed": "That didn’t go through. Please try again.",
          "rate": "[n] out of 5",
          "soldSuffix": " (sold out)",
          "noneSuffix": " (not in this colour)",
          "pack": "Pack of [qty] · [total] · [pct]% off",
          "packPlain": "Pack of [qty] · [total]",
          "off": "[pct]% off",
          "match": {{ vr.match_text | default: 'This clip shows [colour].' | json }},
          "matchPick": {{ vr.match_pick_label | default: 'Choose [colour]' | json }},
          "matchSame": {{ vr.match_same_text | default: 'Same colour as this clip: [colour].' | json }},
          "pause": {{ pause_label | json }},
          "play": {{ play_label | json }},
          "lbPause": "Pause",
          "lbPlay": "Play"
        }
      }
    </script>
  </section>
{%- elsif request.design_mode -%}
  <section class="cvvr cvvr--empty{% if mode == 'inline' %} cvvr--inline{% endif %}" {{ attrs }}>
    <div class="cvvr__inner">
      <div class="cvvr__empty">
        {%- render 'cv-icon', name: 'video', size: 28 -%}
        {%- if show_commerce -%}
          <p><b>Video reviews: no clips for this product yet.</b></p>
          <p>Add a “Video review” block {% if mode == 'inline' %}to this section {% endif %}for each clip a customer sent you: upload the video, then type their name, star rating and review exactly as they gave them. Leave “Only show on” blank to show a clip on every product, or pick the product it belongs to.</p>
          <p>{% if mode == 'inline' %}The row appears here, under the product photo, once this product has a clip. Until then nothing shows on your live store.{% else %}This section stays hidden on your live store until this product has at least one clip.{% endif %}</p>
        {%- else -%}
          <p><b>Video reviews: no clips yet.</b></p>
          <p>Add a “Video review” block to this section for each clip a customer sent you: upload the video, then type their name, star rating and review exactly as they gave them.</p>
          <p>The section appears here once it has a clip. Until then nothing shows on your live store.</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
{%- endif -%}
